      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_9c50012ec31f7d150874dbf25ddb4d3c404647758d30cdb0b7d64f78980fa693",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Optimality in one module need not optimize the full proof. Once extremal approximation is solved, arithmetic cancellation becomes the limiting interface. Robustness across a family of kernels can make a suboptimal construction strategically preferable.",
