    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7d06d043b2681283325ef5d632ae150c4b52c383ea73306aac2f93b9b812a215",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A nonnegative-mixture representation places the scaled logarithmic kernel in the Carneiro-Vaaler class, where half-integer interpolation gives the L1-optimal minorant at fixed exponential type; the subsequent physical- and Fourier-space verification transports that optimum to g_Delta. By contrast, integrating the compactly supported kernels K_Delta and adding a controlled correction produces a valid but nonoptimal minorant. The latter loses the sharp extremal constant yet remains usable for shifted logarithmic kernels that do not lie in the Carneiro-Vaaler framework, exposing a genuine sharpness-versus-portability tradeoff.",
