    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_be8b484c23ddb1f2a8cea95f6baeb7eaf38dd49c498531ce2651a5aeb6e0569d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Under RH, the xi-ratio representation converts log|zeta(1/2+it)| into log t minus a positive sum of the zero-distance kernel f. Replacing f by the ordered entire minorant g_Delta therefore gives an upper bound, while g_Delta's explicit-formula admissibility and compact Fourier support convert that bound into a finite-band prime expression. Its exact L1 deficit supplies the leading log t coefficient, so Delta simultaneously controls approximation loss and arithmetic bandwidth; the interpolation and Fourier calculations are what verify that one function satisfies every required interface condition.",
